hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20315","Hashim and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: One who heard the Bedouin narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying. He said: He raised his head from bowing and raised his hands until they aligned with or reached the branches of his ears, as if they were two fans."
"20316","Hashim and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us from Humayd, he said: And one who heard the Bedouin narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying wearing two sandals of cowhide. He said: He spat to his left, then rubbed where he spat with his sandal."
"20317","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Yazid ibn al-Shikhkhir from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, he said: A Bedouin of ours informed me, he said: I saw the sandal of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) patched."
